  "details": "Now we have many false triggers for, mostly, \"fight\" animations based on contact receivers when people just run into each other.\nI propose to add two checkboxes for OnEnter Contact Recievers:\n-Subtract my velocity\n-Subtract others velocity\nSimply, if you're running with speed 4 (biggest modulo value of VelocityX, Y and Z) into someone, your OnContact has a threshold of 3.0, running into a still sender will result in -1.0, so no trigger shot (instead of 4.0 as of now). Vice versa with others' velocities, they run into you - no trigger.\nOptionally, this should not work for desktop users (desktop users has \"subtract my velocity\" ignored for their avatars; other players' avatars ignore \"subtract others velocity\" when they collide with desktop players) so they still can \"run\" into people since it's the only way for them.\nThat's something like the immobile for locomotion we have on physbones.",
